;; Clojure's read level's divergences (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP1, RPS2, RPS3): the classes
;; of the level's non-passes, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (test/clojure/divergences.edn
;; says how a case is written and matched). The level is both halves (RPS2): Arbace's reader
;; (Clojure's suite's reader and edn, the oracle's reader files: none failing) and repr/clojure's
;; read, whose one-way rules (arbace.repr.clojure.rules, :way :one-way) are cases "one-way RULE:
;; what print cannot restore". Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :one-way-rules
  :title "repr/clojure's one-way rules: a .cljc's conditionals, SecurityManager's spelling"
  :kind :design
  :why "a .cljc read into a .ae keeps the :clj branch only (read --full records the conditionals, printed back byte for byte); read qualifies every SecurityManager, print unqualifies every one (the same class in Clojure)"
  :decided "doc/REPR-CLOJURE.md, \"The one-way rules\""
  :match [#"^one-way :(reader-conditionals|security-manager): "]}
]
